# Pinned SHA-256 of the upstream autopkgtest inputs, taken from
# debian-tag2upload-keyring_1.2.tar.xz
#   sha256 28649310f9fdf5d8d691931196ed45237215ef543afe7a1f5683bcd3fd08a9b8
# which is the value locked in ../conandata.yml.
#
# test_package/upstream/ holds byte-identical copies of these files so the
# upstream test can be executed against the *packaged* keyring (the upstream
# script resolves the keyring as "$PWD/debian-tag2upload.pgp"). The hashes are
# re-checked at test time, so a drifted copy fails loudly instead of silently
# testing something other than what upstream ships.
